From e74c7b3bec6bbfe36a7961d174f02b6c98186dba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:43:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] cryptonote_core: start the index warm-up at the end of
 core::init

core::init calls BlockchainDB::warm_indexes() once, as its last step,
after the database is open and after the rest of core::init (Blockchain
and txpool init, the hard fork state) has read its own tables. In monerod
that is before P2P starts (its constructor binds the ports) and before
RPC, but the warm-up runs in a thread of its own, so neither waits for it.

Why last. Started right after db->open(), the warm-up's read-ahead requests
were ahead of those other reads in the disk queue, and P2P and RPC still
waited for it. On a 12-core Ryzen 9 3900X (16 GB RAM, SATA SSD) with the
stressnet DB out of the page cache, "Core initialized OK" then came only
after the warm-up ended: 4.1 s after "Initializing core" on the SSD instead
of 1.1 s, and 57 s with reads limited to 15 MB/s, the same as
monerodato.5's synchronous warm-up (57 s).

Started last, after those reads, RPC answered 1.4 s after launch on the
SSD and 1.9 s under the limit (monerodato.5: 57 s), while the warm-up
went on to read the same 829 MB in 3.2-5.5 s and 55 s.

The first, synchronous version of the warm-up (monerodato.5) delayed the
node's start by the warm-up: on the stressnet chain about a minute on a
5,400 rpm disk and about 3 s on a SATA SSD (prototype figures). It was
chosen over a background thread for simplicity, and so that the effect
measures cleanly. The sync that follows starts warm in either version.

monero-blockchain-import runs a core, so it warms too. The other tools open
the database directly and do not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_core.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_core.cpp b/src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_core.cpp
index 7d00ca1cc..bc076c1bf 100644
--- a/src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_core.cpp
+++ b/src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_core.cpp
@@ -749,6 +749,11 @@ namespace cryptonote
       }
     }
 
+    // Start reading the hash indexes into the page cache, in the background: much faster than the
+    // random reads a sync would otherwise make for the same pages on a spinning disk. It starts last,
+    // so that the reads above do not queue behind it, and P2P and RPC start without waiting for it
+    m_blockchain_storage.get_db().warm_indexes();
+
     return load_state_data();
   }
   //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
